      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
      ":question/worked-solution": "The line integral of unity with respect to arc length over $C$ is equal to the arc length $L$ of $C,$ i.e.,\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s=L.\n$$\n\nIn this case, the path $C$ is the hypotenuse of a right triangle whose legs have lengths $6$ and $8:$ \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/generate/scratch/17592186162081/assets/2b9ca69d9e868fc9f79e23434b71d8224694d89471155e097d6127a4296c3381.png)\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & =\\sqrt{{6}^{2}+{8}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{36+64} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{100} \\\\  & =10.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s=10.\n$$"
    },
