      ":question/worked-solution": "The line integral of unity with respect to arc length over $C$ is equal to the arc length $L$ of $C,$ i.e.,\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s=L.\n$$\n\nIn this case, the path $C$ is the hypotenuse of a right triangle whose legs have lengths $\\frac{7}{2}$ and $\\frac{11}{2}:$ \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/generate/scratch/17592186162081/assets/01185ac87e90b7b49f8514d0343a5b82dd5a8e43668b00570470ea1c7c68a8c6.png)\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & =\\sqrt{{\\frac{7}{2}}^{2}+{\\frac{11}{2}}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{49}{4}+\\frac{121}{4}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{85}{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{170}}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s=\\frac{\\sqrt{170}}{2}.\n$$"
