      ":question/worked-solution": "The line integral of unity with respect to arc length over $C$ is equal to the arc length $L$ of $C,$ i.e.,\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s=L.\n$$\n\nIn this case, the path $C$ is the hypotenuse of a right triangle whose legs have lengths $\\frac{19}{3}$ and $\\frac{21}{4}:$ \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/generate/scratch/17592186162081/assets/37cd7f2255ceeafe2046a3ecb5464c3c14cf5a90acfa12f7fa78a75bf215076b.png)\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & =\\sqrt{{\\frac{19}{3}}^{2}+{\\frac{21}{4}}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{361}{9}+\\frac{441}{16}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{9745}{144}} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{9745}}{12}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s=\\frac{\\sqrt{9745}}{12}.\n$$"
