      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/hard",
      ":question/worked-solution": "The line integral of unity with respect to arc length over $C$ is equal to the arc length $L$ of $C,$ i.e.,\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s=L.\n$$\n\nIn this case, the path $C$ is the hypotenuse of a right triangle whose legs have lengths $\\frac{10}{3}$ and $\\frac{23}{4}:$ \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/generate/scratch/17592186162081/assets/07d717012039fa5389408c14b5a67fe5ebfeaf9cd53c915297861f9adb40adde.png)\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & =\\sqrt{{\\frac{10}{3}}^{2}+{\\frac{23}{4}}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{100}{9}+\\frac{529}{16}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{6361}{144}} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{6361}}{12}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s=\\frac{\\sqrt{6361}}{12}.\n$$"
